-- AT-201 part 1: `payments` becomes the Web POS tender record — one row per
-- payment ATTEMPT, not per order. Spec: docs/FAVO_PRD_v7.md §10.3 (payments
-- row), §10.3.3 (the field list), §10.6 (the two partial unique indexes),
-- §6.8.4 (no void), L02 (no refunds). Generated by drizzle-kit from
-- db/schema.ts + db/enums.ts, then hand-edited where noted.
--
--   1. order_id NULL-able; fund_topup_id (new; FK to donor_fund_entries added
--      when that table exists); CHECK num_nonnulls(order_id, fund_topup_id) = 1
--   2. attempt, client_reference (UNIQUE), webpos_device_id, charged_amount_zar,
--      fee_zar (NULL, never 0, while unknown), receipt_no, settlement_ref,
--      sent_at, last_checked_at, at. No tip column (DEC-17).
--   3. payment_status rebuilt to exactly pending | successful | declined |
--      unresolved. failed -> declined. `refunded` and `deferred` are dropped;
--      `voided` is never added.
--   4. payments_one_successful_per_fund_topup (COL-5), beside the order index.
--   5. UNIQUE(order_id, attempt) — attempt is "1, 2, 3 … per order".
--
-- Renumbered 0035 -> 0043 to follow merge order (0034..0042 landed on main
-- first; orders.notification_target is 0042, PR #284); the SQL statements are
-- unchanged apart from the migration number in the two refusal messages and
-- the removal of #285's tip_zar column (DEC-17, 22 Oct 2026: no tip column).
--
-- Hand edits: (a) a guard that refuses, touching nothing, if any row is
-- `refunded` or `deferred` — neither has a truthful target value, so no row is
-- guessed at; (b) the NOT NULL columns are added nullable, backfilled, then set
-- NOT NULL, so this also applies to a table with rows (PRD §13.0 says FAVO
-- starts clean, where every UPDATE touches zero rows); (c) the enum swap drops
-- and re-creates the order index and the status default around it, and maps
-- failed -> declined. Legacy backfill: attempt = 1, 2, … per order, oldest
-- first. 0033's payments has no creation time; its only per-row time is
-- webhook_received_at, so rows order by that (unanswered rows last), then id;
-- client_reference = 'legacy:' || order_id || ':' || attempt (orders has no
-- client_uuid yet); webpos_device_id = 'legacy:yoco-online-checkout' (those
-- rows came from Yoco Online, which has no Web POS device); at = the order's
-- placed_at. charged_amount_zar and sent_at stay NULL: never recorded, so not
-- invented. The reverse is drizzle/down/0043_at201_tender_payments.down.sql.
-- favo:requires-approval rebuilds payments: drops and re-creates the payment_status enum and the one-successful index, backfills new NOT NULL columns with UPDATEs

DO $$
BEGIN
  IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM "payments" WHERE "status"::text IN ('refunded', 'deferred')) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'AT-201/0043: payments holds refunded or deferred rows, which have no v7 status — not migrating, nothing changed';
  END IF;
END $$;--> statement-breakpoint
